    "title": {
     "en": "Kishan's nursery"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Kishan runs a plant nursery. Villagers take saplings from him. He had 364 saplings and brought 52 more from a friend's village. How many does he have now?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "rupee",
     "note",
     "coin",
     "saplings"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Give and Take is about adding and subtracting three-digit numbers in real stories.\nKishan had 364 saplings and brought 52 more. We add: 364 + 52.\nAdd ones: 4 + 2 = 6. Add tens: 6 + 5 = 11 tens, which is 1 hundred and 1 ten. Add hundreds: 3 + 1 = 4. The total is 416 saplings.\nA box diagram helps: draw a box for 364, a box for 52 and a big box for the total.\nYou can also use a number line, jumping from 364 by tens.\nMoney also uses hundreds, tens and ones. A ₹100 note, a ₹10 note and a ₹1 coin work like hundreds, tens and ones.\nMake play money and practice exchanging ten ₹10 notes for one ₹100 note."
    }
   },
